Subject: [PATCH] Fix Jitsi bridge load balancer exposure

---
 README.md                       |  5 +++--
 manifests/jitsi-colibri-ws.yaml | 13 ++++++++++++-
 manifests/metallb-l2.yaml       |  9 +--------
 manifests/metallb-pool.yaml     |  9 +--------
 scripts/02-install-jitsi.sh     | 19 +++++++++++++------
 scripts/04-create-hosts.sh      |  6 +++---
 values/jitsi-values.yaml        |  8 ++++++--
 7 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e1f928f..2253524 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,9 +9,10 @@ Internal Jitsi Meet deployment on a 2-node k8s cluster.
 | srv-deploy-eng  | 192.168.20.180 | control-plane |
 | jenkins         | 192.168.20.177 | worker        |
 
-- LoadBalancer IP: `192.168.20.190` (MetalLB)
-- Access: `https://vidcall3.internal`
+- LoadBalancer IP: `192.168.20.190` (MetalLB, shared by ingress-nginx TCP/443 and JVB UDP/31829)
+- Access: `https://vidcall3-prod.transmedika.co.id`
 - Auth: internal (Prosody users)
+- Public JVB IP advertised to clients: `157.15.164.236`
 
 ## Prerequisites
 
diff --git a/manifests/jitsi-colibri-ws.yaml b/manifests/jitsi-colibri-ws.yaml
index 7511141..c542635 100644
--- a/manifests/jitsi-colibri-ws.yaml
+++ b/manifests/jitsi-colibri-ws.yaml
@@ -1,3 +1,14 @@
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: ConfigMap
+metadata:
